# Logseq db schema + built-in rules (file-based graphs)
# Attribute names for advanced queries. DB-version renames: logseq/db-version
# https://github.com/logseq/logseq/blob/0.10.9/deps/db/src/logseq/db/schema.cljs

## A page is just a block that has :block/name.

## Block attributes
:db/id                          entity id (what :current-block resolves to)
:block/uuid                     the ((...)) reference id      unique
:block/content                  full text of the block
:block/format                   :markdown or :org
:block/page             ref     the page this block lives on
:block/parent           ref     parent block
:block/left             ref     previous sibling (ordering)
:block/collapsed?
:block/pre-block?               first block of a page, i.e. frontmatter
:block/refs             ref many  pages/blocks this block references
:block/path-refs        ref many  refs inherited from ancestors too
:block/tags             ref many
:block/macros           ref many
:block/marker                   "TODO" "DOING" "NOW" "LATER" "DONE" ...
:block/priority                 "A" "B" "C"
:block/scheduled                yyyymmdd integer
:block/deadline                 yyyymmdd integer
:block/repeated?
:block/properties               map: key -> set of refs (or raw text)
:block/properties-order         vector of keys
:block/properties-text-values   map: key -> original text
:block/created-at               ms timestamp
:block/updated-at               ms timestamp
:block/type                     "whiteboard", "macros", ...
:block/file             ref

## Page-only attributes
:block/name                     lower-cased page name       unique
:block/original-name            as typed                    unique
:block/journal?                 true for journal pages
:block/journal-day              20210529 style integer
:block/namespace        ref     parent page of `parent/child`
:block/alias            ref many

## File attributes
:file/path (unique)   :file/content   :file/handle

## Built-in rules (usable in :where without declaring them)
(task ?b #{"TODO" "DOING"})        marker in the set
(priority ?b #{"A"})               priority in the set
(between ?b ?start ?end)           block is on a journal page in the range
(page ?b ?page-name)               block belongs to a named page
(page-ref ?b ?page-name)           block or an ancestor references the page
(block-content ?b ?substring)      substring of :block/content
(property ?b ?key ?val)            block property equals / contains
(has-property ?b ?key)             block has the property at all
(page-property ?p ?key ?val)       page property
(has-page-property ?p ?key)
(page-tags ?p #{"tag"})            page tagged with any of these
(all-page-tags ?p)                 ?p is used as a tag somewhere
(namespace ?p ?namespace)          direct parent namespace of a page
# From logseq.db.rules; property values are sets, so use #{...} for the
# marker/priority/tag arguments.

## Recursive rules (pass via :rules, they are not on by default)
[(namespace ?p ?c) [?c :block/namespace ?p]]
[(namespace ?p ?c) [?t :block/namespace ?p] (namespace ?t ?c)]
[(alias ?e2 ?e1) [?e2 :block/alias ?e1]]
[(alias ?e2 ?e1) [?e1 :block/alias ?e2]]
